# Walk through the whole flow. Run the requests top to bottom; the ids flow from one response to the next.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Start a draft order
# @name start
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{$guid}}", "currency": "EUR" }

### 2. Add a line
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "BOOK-1984", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 12.50, "currency": "EUR" }

### 3. A business rule says no: wrong currency -> 422 with code order.currency-mismatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "PEN-BLUE", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 2.00, "currency": "USD" }

### 4. Input that can never be valid: quantity 0 -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "PEN-BLUE", "quantity": 0, "unitPrice": 2.00, "currency": "EUR" }

### 5. Place the order: raises OrderPlaced, stores the integration event in the outbox
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}/place
Content-Type: application/json

{ "street": "Main Street 1", "postalCode": "1234 AB", "city": "Springfield", "countryCode": "NL" }

### 6. Shipping prepared a shipment (a moment after the outbox published)
# @name shipments
GET {{baseUrl}}/shipments?orderId={{start.response.body.$.id}}

### 7. Dispatch it: Shipping publishes ShipmentDispatched, Ordering marks the order shipped
POST {{baseUrl}}/shipments/{{shipments.response.body.$[0].id}}/dispatch
Content-Type: application/json

{ "trackingCode": "TRACK12345NL" }

### 8. The order is now Shipped
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}

### 9. Too late to cancel -> 422 with code order.already-shipped
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{start.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Changed my mind" }
